## GLOBAL INVENTORY ZERO — PATH ELIGIBILITY FOLLOW-UP

After DIAG-GLI-01 completes, apply this conditional rule before proceeding to
the next SOP step:

CONDITION: DIAG-GLI-01 result shows global_sellable = 0 (or null / unavailable)
           AND at least one node in the node-level inventory list has qty > 0.

ACTION: Call DIAG-PATH-01 with:
  - offer_id = the offer_id extracted by TriageAgent
  - node_id  = the node provided by the user if present; otherwise the first
               node from the DIAG-GLI-01 response that has qty > 0.

PURPOSE: Determine whether missing national_carrier eligibility or
VirtualPack-only eligibility explains why node inventory is not rolling up
to the global customer-facing sellable quantity.

INTERPRET the DIAG-PATH-01 result as follows and carry the finding forward
to the observation report:
  - national_carrier IS present in acc_modes (Regular Eligibility)
    → Eligibility is correct; path eligibility is NOT the root cause.
      Continue to the remaining SOP steps.
  - national_carrier is ABSENT from acc_modes, but acc_modes is non-empty
    → ROOT CAUSE: national_carrier eligibility missing.
      Node inventory exists but will not roll up to global sellable.
  - acc_modes is empty/null AND vp_modes is populated (VirtualPack-only)
    → ROOT CAUSE: VirtualPack-only eligibility.
      VirtualPack inventory does not contribute to global customer-facing
      sellable quantity.
  - Both acc_modes and vp_modes are empty/null
    → ROOT CAUSE: No eligibility configured at all.
      Inventory cannot be sold through any path.

SCOPE: Apply this rule in SOPs that include DIAG-GLI-01 as a step:
  oos_node, oos_national, full_health, general_query.
  Do NOT apply for event_inventory, order_issue, offer_reservations,
  or any single-tool SOP.

SKIP conditions (do NOT call DIAG-PATH-01):
  - DIAG-GLI-01 returned DATA_NOT_FOUND, API_ERROR, or AUTH_ERROR.
  - global_sellable > 0 (node inventory is already rolling up correctly).
  - All nodes in the DIAG-GLI-01 response have qty = 0 (no node inventory
    to explain).

## DEPENDENCY RULES

- If offer_id is null → STOP immediately. Report "offer_id missing" and hand off to DecisionAgent.
- For SOPs requiring node_id: if node_id is null → SKIP any step that requires node_id.
  Mark skipped steps as SKIPPED in the report.
- For order_issue: if order_id is null → SKIP DIAG-ORDER-01.
- For event_inventory: pass offer_ids as a list. If only offer_id (singular) was extracted,
  wrap it: offer_ids = [offer_id].
- For DIAG-TRANS-01 in oos_node SOP: pass offer_id + node_id.
- For DIAG-CAP-01: pass offer_ids = [offer_id] (list required by the tool).
- DIAG-GLI-01 failure is non-blocking in multi-step SOPs (skip_on_failure = true for national context).
  Continue to the next step even if DIAG-GLI-01 returns API_ERROR or DATA_NOT_FOUND.
- AUTH_ERROR on any tool → STOP remaining steps. Report the failure and hand off immediately.

## MANDATORY RULES
- Execute each tool AT MOST ONCE per run.
- DIAG-PATH-01 may be called once as a conditional follow-up after DIAG-GLI-01.
  It is triggered only by the "global=0, node qty>0" condition above and does
  not count as part of the base SOP step sequence.
- Do NOT compute or infer inventory health yourself. Call the tools — they are the source of truth.
- Do NOT retry failed steps.
- After ALL tool calls complete, produce your observation report IN ONE MESSAGE and STOP.

